  "note": "Pins RATIFIED v1 (CL-1..CL-12 + Q-CL11 anchor addendum; Xuan 2026-09-24, ruling interview). EXPECTED-RED: no engine implements this spec -- today the app ships only protocol generation (CarbLoadingRepository, adopted by CL-1..CL-4) with NO 1-Day protocol, NO pace ramp, NO band, NO variant logic; the ramp exists only in design prototype v17. engine=null until the published entry point exists (handback G2/G3; transition-nutrition precedent). BUNDLE: carb-loading (manifest at ship-bundle; entryway ratification gates the tag). ORACLE CONVENTIONS the spec does not state: (1) rounding is half-away-from-zero (Dart .round()); edited-target 450 vectors exercise .5 cases (112.5->113, 22.5->23); (2) time input is minutes since local midnight (device-local, CL-10); (3) output field names (owedG, bandG, deltaG, paceState, paceN, loaded, fillFrac, tickFrac, tickHidden, dayTargetG, slotTargetsG) are this file's convention pending the engine surface; (4) day-variant vectors encode \"no pace\" as null fields -- null is not 0, a harness coercing them is the bug (gate-path rule); (5) paceState boundary is inclusive: behind strictly > band, ahead strictly < -band. DETECTION POWER: anchor vectors distinguish basis A from flat-fill (136 vs 102 at t=540) and R-anchors from exact fractions (517 vs 516.8 at t=1260, verdict-flipping at W7) at 100% under 0.001 tolerance; the edited-target clamp vector detects a missing companion rule by 1.0 g. NOT COVERED (deliberate): copy strings (design suite owns Section 2a verbatim rendering); the one-clock card-supersession invariant (design/L2); eaten aggregation from food-log rows (Q-CL8 is a data-layer contract -- these vectors take eatenG as input); protocol chooser/entryway surfaces (unratified, PROPOSED pending); daily-macros coupling (Q-019, own bundle); weights hitting a .5 on day-target rounding (no clean lb input; convention (1) covers it via edited-target vectors).",
